      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While fixing our own economy is vital, the critics' belief that we must do so in isolation before helping others is fundamentally shortsighted, as global instability directly threatens our domestic prosperity. Ignoring the urgent needs of the world only fosters insecurity, extremism, and displacement that will inevitably flow back across our borders to destabilize our very own infrastructure. True strength lies not in isolationism but in the shared understanding that lifting the global ledger of suffering creates a safer, more stable future for all, including ourselves.",
      "source": "target",
