      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a strong way to frame it. It really leans into the \"self-interest\" angle which helps. One more thing—some people argue that foreign aid is often just lost to corruption and doesn't actually reach the people it's meant for, making the whole moral argument moot. How can I shut down that argument in the speech? I want to make it clear that the corruption argument is just a bad excuse to stop helping people.",
